WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:03.922
"I don't want to be evaporated!" Ally cried.

2
00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:11.287
"I'll miss my friends. And my job. And . . . I'll never see my parents ever again!"

3
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:14.695
"Your reaction is illogical," Alpha said.

4
00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:18.057
"No, it's not," Ally said.

5
00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:22.288
"Recall your life-form studies from fourth grade," Alpha said.

6
00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.053
"Remember what you were taught about Jorgandians?"

7
00:00:26.054 --> 00:00:35.549
"Um." Ally paused. "I think I was absent that day."

8
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:41.984
"Negative!" Alpha snapped. "My records indicate you were present for that lesson."

9
00:00:41.985 --> 00:00:48.169
"Fine!" Ally sighed. "I guess I wasn't paying attention.

10
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.557
Can you please just tell me what I need to know about Jorgandians?"

11
00:00:52.558 --> 00:01:00.290
"In the galactic year 874303, the Jorgandians vowed to destroy Astralia," Alpha said.

12
00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:07.305
"They despise the Astralians' peaceful way because it interferes with their goal of taking over the galaxy.

13
00:01:07.306 --> 00:01:16.026
Recently they developed a dangerous weapon—a small disk capable of instantly evaporating an Astralian life-form."

14
00:01:16.027 --> 00:01:22.018
"Jorgandians sound awful!" Mateo said. "What else, Alpha?"

15
00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:24.727
"They can move extremely fast.

16
00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:29.015
They are sly and wear a device much like your meld medallion.

17
00:01:29.016 --> 00:01:33.562
But their device enables them to take over other life-forms."

18
00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:37.125
"What does that mean?" Mateo asked.

19
00:01:37.126 --> 00:01:43.789
"It means, they can inhabit another life-form's body."

20
00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.899
Ally had to sit down; her legs were shaking so badly.

21
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.966
"Correct," Alpha said.

22
00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:57.541
"The inhabited life-form looks and sounds much like its normal self, but the Jorgandian controls its every move."

23
00:01:57.542 --> 00:02:02.293
"So . . ." Mateo dropped down next to Ally, looking worried.

24
00:02:02.294 --> 00:02:06.774
"We won't be able to tell the Jorgandian from a real human?"

25
00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:09.608
"Correc—" Alpha's screen blinked off.

26
00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:12.352
Seconds later she started up again.

27
00:02:12.353 --> 00:02:18.057
"Oh no, Alpha, you're still glitching." Ally felt like crying.

28
00:02:18.058 --> 00:02:22.713
"We'll never be able to find the Jorgandian before it finds me!"

29
00:02:22.714 --> 00:02:24.959
"Incorrect," Alpha said.

30
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:32.153
"While my systems are unstable in this primitive device, you can use your Astralian abilities to locate the Jorgandian."

31
00:02:32.154 --> 00:02:36.545
Mateo nodded. "All we have to do is walk around town, Ally!

32
00:02:36.546 --> 00:02:42.803
You can read the minds of everyone we pass. We'll find the Jorgandian in no time."

33
00:02:42.804 --> 00:02:49.986
"No, we won't," Ally said. "If it spots me first, I'll be evaporated."

34
00:02:49.987 --> 00:02:52.481
She jumped up and started pacing.

35
00:02:52.482 --> 00:02:58.205
"We have to figure out where the life-form is before I can leave the house again."

36
00:02:58.206 --> 00:03:03.336
Alpha displayed a map of Sandville. "The life-form is within this area.

37
00:03:03.337 --> 00:03:07.460
But I haven't been able to pinpoint its precise location."

38
00:03:07.461 --> 00:03:10.803
"That's a pretty big area," Mateo said.

39
00:03:10.804 --> 00:03:14.874
"It goes from Pepe's all the way to the copy shop."

40
00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:19.488
"Wait!" Ally halted. "It's Melanie!"

41
00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:22.984
Mateo frowned. "Why do you think that?"

42
00:03:22.985 --> 00:03:27.533
"Because she made me a Galorpian astroshake," Ally said.

43
00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:34.022
"And she said she had a necklace that was similar to my meld medallion."

44
00:03:34.023 --> 00:03:40.034
"I don't know. Melanie seems harmless, and Papi says she's a good worker.

45
00:03:40.035 --> 00:03:44.581
Maybe those things are just coincidences," Mateo said.

46
00:03:44.582 --> 00:03:47.992
"What do you think, Alpha?" Ally asked.

47
00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:52.416
"Jorgandians do love Galorpian food," Alpha said.

48
00:03:52.417 --> 00:03:58.311
"How am I supposed to work beside a Jorgandian?" Ally wrung her hands.

49
00:03:58.312 --> 00:04:04.722
"I'm in so much danger! Why didn't I pay better attention in school?"

50
00:04:04.723 --> 00:04:11.454
Alpha snorted. "If you had listened, Allyzooba, you would have remembered something important:

51
00:04:11.455 --> 00:04:14.785
Jorgandians have a powerful evaporation weapon.

52
00:04:14.786 --> 00:04:19.055
But they will not use it on you as long as humans are around.

53
00:04:19.056 --> 00:04:23.114
They fear humans would get alarmed, and possibly violent."

54
00:04:23.115 --> 00:04:29.319
"Phew!" Ally said. "I'll be safe as long as humans are around.

55
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.077
But I can't avoid being alone with Melanie forever.

56
00:04:33.078 --> 00:04:38.473
I need a plan for throwing her off my trail, and I need one fast!"

57
00:04:38.474 --> 00:04:43.759
"What do Astralians do when they meet Jorgandians in space?" Mateo asked.

58
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.064
"How do you fight them?"

59
00:04:46.065 --> 00:04:50.438
"We don't fight anyone, ever," Ally said.

60
00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:56.960
"Astralian cloaking devices protect our ships and planet from attack.

61
00:04:56.961 --> 00:05:02.972
If I still had my pod, I could stay in there, but . . ." She sighed.

62
00:05:02.973 --> 00:05:07.637
"That's long gone."

63
00:05:07.638 --> 00:05:10.930
"I have an idea!" Mateo brightened.

64
00:05:10.931 --> 00:05:15.663
"You can ask Dr. Lloyd for help in finding the Jorgandian.

65
00:05:15.664 --> 00:05:22.164
His alien beacon doesn't work, but maybe he's working on a new experiment to attract aliens."

66
00:05:22.165 --> 00:05:25.073
"Dr. Lloyd?" Ally shook her head.

67
00:05:25.074 --> 00:05:31.641
"No way! If he can detect a Jorgandian in town, then he'll detect me too!"

68
00:05:31.642 --> 00:05:35.147
"Allyzooba is correct," Alpha said.

69
00:05:35.148 --> 00:05:38.111
"It's up to us," Ally said.

70
00:05:38.112 --> 00:05:43.269
Ally wanted to come up with a plan, but she suddenly felt very tired.

71
00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.393
She sank onto her bed, yawning.

72
00:05:46.394 --> 00:05:49.557
"You must be exhausted from your trip.

73
00:05:49.558 --> 00:05:54.066
Get some rest; it will help you think more clearly," Mateo said.

74
00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:59.971
"Good idea." Ally yawned again.

75
00:05:59.972 --> 00:06:07.472
"See you in the morning."

